[tool_use] Agent {"description":"Strategy plan for Phase 6 decomposition","subagent_type":"strategy-planner","prompt":"You are planning the decomposition of Phase 6 (Video Opponent Mode) for the pointfight-reactor project. The project is at `/home/aaron/dev/projects/aaron/pointfight-reactor`. Phases 1-5 + 2b.1-2b.4 are shipped and approved. Phase 6 is the next unapproved phase.\n\n**Phase 6 acceptance criteria (from docs/PHASES.md):**\n- User can import local clips.\n- User can tag cue type and cue timestamp.\n- App can randomly play clips.\n- Reaction timer starts from cue timestamp.\n- Results are stored by clip and cue type.\n\n**Context to read:**\n- `docs/PHASES.md` — Phase 6 section + how Phase 2b was decomposed into 2b.1-2b.4 (your decomposition should follow the same pattern: small sub-phases each independently verifiable + reviewable)\n- `docs/SPEC.md` §\"Cue Representation\", §\"Cue Types\"\n- `artifacts/decision-memo.md` — read the existing memo to understand the project's planning idiom (it's currently 35KB and contains all prior decomposition memos)\n- `app/src/engine/` — drill engine (session.ts, scheduler.ts, types.ts, profile.ts) so you understand how cues, timing, and SessionRecord/RepRecord flow today\n- `app/src/cues/` — existing data-driven cue palette from Phase 3 (you'll want to reuse it for cue tagging)\n- `app/src/store/` — Zustand stores + Dexie persistence (db.ts) so you understand the existing storage layer\n- `app/src/ui/` — screens to understand where a clip-import / tagging screen would slot in\n\n**Your task — produce a Phase 6 decomposition decision memo addition.** Append to `artifacts/decision-memo.md` (do NOT rewrite the file) a new section titled `## Phase 6 decomposition memo — Video Opponent Mode`.\n\nCover:\n1. **Storage strategy** — clips can be 10-100MB H.264 .mp4 files. Strategies: (a) store Blob in IndexedDB via Dexie (works offline, ~bounded by browser quota ~10% of disk), (b) URL.createObjectURL on import + ephemeral look