[text] Phase 6 planning iteration complete. Stopping per operating rules — the outer loop will commit and the next iteration picks up Phase 6.1 implementation.

**What changed:**
- `artifacts/decision-memo.md` — appended Phase 6 decomposition memo (3 sub-phases, storage / tagging / playback / RT / results / risks), an adversarial red-team review (1 ACCEPTED + 8 MODIFY + 1 BLOCK with quoted source-line citations), and a resolution section that locks each finding in as a concrete acceptance criterion.
- `docs/PHASES.md:182` — Phase 6 replaced with the 6.1 / 6.2 / 6.3 breakdown; original acceptance criteria preserved for traceability; each sub-phase has falsifiable per-criterion test obligations.
- `docs/QUALITY_GATES.md:45` — `Browser-API limitations` section extended with a Phase 6 entry (HTML5 `<video>`, `requestVideoFrameCallback`, `navigator.storage.estimate`) mirroring the Phase 2b §B1–§B4 shape.
- `artifacts/phase-update.json` — written as the signal artifact (action=decompose, approved=false, next_phase=6.1).

**Key lock-ins from red-team resolution:**
- 6.3 ships an extracted `engine/persistence.ts:commitRep()` so `session.ts` and the new `clipmode/runner.ts` share rep-commit invariants (DRY-gate compliance).
- Dexie v4 schema declaration enumerated explicitly with a v3→v4 upgrade survival test.
- `addClip()` returns a typed `{ ok, reason }` result with a 200 MB per-clip hard cap and a stubbed `QuotaExceededError` test.
- Clip mode is feature-gated on `requestVideoFrameCallback` — Safari < 15.4 sees a disabled-with-banner state, eliminating cross-browser RT incoherence.
- Random clip selection is pinned to uniform-with-replacement + no-repeat-immediately-previous, with a ±20 % bounded distribution test.
- 6.3 approval sets `project_complete: true`; the iteration after writes `artifacts/project-complete.json` with `final_phase: "6.3", deferred: ["phase-7"]`.

**Verification:** lint clean, tsc clean, 190/190 vitest tests pass, vite build clean (matches Phase 2b.4 baseline since no code changed).
